===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno}} and {{etyl|frm}} {{term|oyez|lang=xno}}, {{term|oiez}}, imperative plural of {{term|oir||to hear}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|oïr||to hear|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|audio|audiō|to hear|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈəʊˌjeɪ/|lang=en}}, {{SAMPA|/"@U.jeI/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|o|yez|lang=en}}
{{rfap||UK}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# [[hear ye|Hear ye]]. Attend. (Called by public [[crier]]s or in [[court]] usually three times to secure silence).

====Usage notes====
* Practise note: It is still used in the United States Supreme Court, and in many state supreme courts, although lower courts seem to have dropped its use.

